  "description": "<p>While trying to determine if Fedora supported unicode in binary filenames, I have seen some inconsistent behaviors. This applies to fedora 5 and 6.</p>\n\n<p>Putting some chinese characters directly in as the filename gives good results in the response Content-Disposition, but not the binary description:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\ncurl -H<span class=\"code-quote\">'Link: &lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//www.w3.org/ns/ldp#NonRDFSource&gt;; rel=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"type\"</span>'</span> --data-binary @README.md -H<span class=\"code-quote\">'Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"浅顶软呢帽岩石\"</span>'</span> -H<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Content-type: text/plain\"</span> -XPOST http://localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/ -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin\r\n</span>\r\ncurl -I http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/90703ac5-191e-48d8-84a9-17300e490520 -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin\r\n</span>\r\n# Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"浅顶软呢帽岩石\"</span>; creation-date=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Thu, 15 Apr 2021 21:00:28 GMT\"</span>; modification-date=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Thu, 15 Apr 2021 21:00:28 GMT\"</span>; size=4719\r\n\r\ncurl http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/90703ac5-191e-48d8-84a9-17300e490520/fcr:metadata -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin\r\n</span>\r\n&lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/90703ac5-191e-48d8-84a9-17300e490520&gt;\r\n</span>        ebucore:filename         \"æµé¡¶è½¯å&lsquo;¢å¸½å²©ç³\" ;\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>You are supposed to be able to define the encoding of the filename using \"Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8...\" form (note, it is filename* rather than filename), but this is simply ignored by fedora. In FedoraLdp it actually parses within the contentDisposition object, but the filename* value is stored as a parameter instead of as the filename, so its not found by the controller code.</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\ncurl -H<span class=\"code-quote\">'Link: &lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//www.w3.org/ns/ldp#NonRDFSource&gt;; rel=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"type\"</span>'</span> --data-binary @README.md -H<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''%e6%b5%85%e9%a1%b6%e8%bd%af%e5%91%a2%e5%b8%bd%e5%b2%a9%e7%9f%b3\"</span> -H<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Content-type: text/plain\"</span> -XPOST http://localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/ -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin\r\n</span>\r\ncurl -I http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/058ac0ce-ecf6-4afe-9b18-f68e5c8e5da3 -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin\r\n</span>\r\n# Content-Disposition: attachment; creation-date=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Thu, 15 Apr 2021 21:07:16 GMT\"</span>; modification-date=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Thu, 15 Apr 2021 21:07:16 GMT\"</span>; size=4719\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>",
